# Repo roles

Two checkouts share this product. Put the change in the repo that owns that kind of work.

| Work | Repo | Path |
|------|------|------|
| Servers, Docker, containers, identity, annotation, export, OData, segmentation, section correction | **Viking** | `d:\src\git\Viking` |
| Clients (Viking, VikingAU, Jotunn, MonogameTestbed, shared client libraries) | **VikingLegacy** | `d:\src\git\VikingLegacy` |

## Keep clients in parallel

Viking still has a `Clients/` tree. Keep it aligned with VikingLegacy so the two can merge later.

- Land client changes in **VikingLegacy** first.
- Mirror the same change into Viking `Clients/` (and any shared client projects it touches) on a best-effort basis in the same piece of work.
- If a client fix is made in Viking, mirror it back into VikingLegacy the same way.
- Do not let the two client trees drift when the mirror is practical in the same change.

Server and container changes stay in Viking. Do not start that work in VikingLegacy.

```text
Jotunn panel change
  → edit Clients/Jotunn in VikingLegacy
  → mirror the same edit under Clients/ in Viking

IdentityServer compose / cert change
  → edit Servers/ in Viking only
```
